      "writtenOn": "2026-02-20T01:18:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see context_get_address_root() is used in exactly one place, and the code around it looks like this:\n```\n#ifdef __PKVM_HYP__\n        if (sm) {\n                pasid_dir \u003d __pkvm_va(context-\u003elo \u0026 VTD_PAGE_MASK);\n                pasid_dir_sz \u003d get_pasid_dir_size(context);\n                if (pasid_table_has_present_entries(pasid_dir, pasid_dir_sz)) {\n                        spin_unlock(\u0026iommu-\u003elock);\n                        return;\n                }\n        } else {\n                pgd \u003d __pkvm_va(context_get_address_root(context));\n        }\n#endif\n```\n\nSo maybe it\u0027s a bit an overkill to add this helper just for this, instead of just open-coding `context-\u003elo \u0026 VTD_PAGE_MASK` like for scalable mode above?",
      "revId": "90c3a2fea087cd3d2c626aa5c5fbc0d05007ea53",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ff8f1afb_978001cd",
        "filename": "drivers/iommu/intel/iommu.h",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 1166,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-20T01:18:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "READ_ONCE doesn\u0027t seem really needed (context entries are only updated by SW, not by HW, and only with iommu-\u003elock held)? \n\nI know it is used a lot in pasid.h, but as noted for example by Jason in https://lore.kernel.org/linux-iommu/20260105191410.GJ125261@ziepe.ca/, there is no real reason for using it there either, it is just historical.\n\nSo for pasid_get_{flptr,slptr}() we might follow this \"pattern\" of using READ_ONCE just because it exists in pasid.h, but here for context entries we don\u0027t need to introduce it?",
      "revId": "90c3a2fea087cd3d2c626aa5c5fbc0d05007ea53",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
